{
  "id": "21338_torinogasu",
  "headword": "{取|と}り{逃|のが}す",
  "reading": "とりのがす",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (godan, transitive)",
  "gloss": "to miss catching; to let escape; to fail to obtain",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to miss catching; to let escape; to fail to seize",
      "explanation": "To fail to catch or capture something or someone that was within reach. Used for criminals, opportunities, and things one tried but failed to get."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "21338_torinogasu_ex1",
      "japanese": "{犯人|はんにん}を{取|と}り{逃|のが}した。",
      "english": "They let the criminal escape.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "21338_torinogasu_ex2",
      "japanese": "チャンスを{取|と}り{逃|のが}してしまった。",
      "english": "I missed the opportunity.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "21338_torinogasu_ex3",
      "japanese": "{限定|げんてい}{商品|しょうひん}を{取|と}り{逃|のが}さないように{早|はや}めに{並|なら}んだ。",
      "english": "I lined up early so as not to miss the limited-edition product.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Compound verb of {取|と}る (to take, to catch) + {逃|のが}す (to let escape, to miss). Godan verb conjugating on the す row. Implies that one had a chance to obtain or capture something but failed.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {犯人|はんにん}を{取|と}り{逃|のが}す: to let a criminal escape\n- チャンスを{取|と}り{逃|のが}す: to miss an opportunity\n- {獲物|えもの}を{取|と}り{逃|のが}す: to let prey escape\n- {勝利|しょうり}を{取|と}り{逃|のが}す: to let victory slip away\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {逃|のが}す: to miss, to let escape (simpler; the base verb)\n- {見逃|みのが}す: to overlook, to miss seeing\n- {乗|の}り{遅|おく}れる: to miss (a vehicle — train, bus)",
